<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Lower bids stifle selling.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Lower bids stifle selling.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A drop in dark northern spring wheat cash bids stifled farmer selling on Thursday, several cash merchandisers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It was just another dead day,&quot; one Minnesota dealer said. &quot;The board collapsed late and that pretty much ended any hope of buying wheat today.&quot;</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures crumbled in late dealings on fund selling and spillover weakness from a break in CBOT wheat.</p>
<p>Weather patterns continued to raise concerns as temperatures remained below normal across much of the spring wheat belt, merchants said.  </p>
